PATCH 387: SETTINGS SMOKE-EFFECTS toggle -- LED re-renders OFF (store-width, patch-318/319 class).

Clicking SMOKE EFFECTS toggled the state + status line ("SMOKE EFFECTS DISABLED") correctly but the LED
indicator stayed lit: the port drew the checked box every frame regardless of the flipped flag.

ROOT (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin; the exact class patches 318/319 fixed for SKY + the
radios): the SMOKE checkbox's two flags were left WORD-typed while the 318/319 sweep retyped the
neighbours -- 0x8bb5 sits between the 319-fixed 0x8bb2 and 0x8bbb and was SKIPPED.
  - SMOKE widget DIRTY flag 0x8bb5 (DAT_2000_4bb5): asm 0x6c22 `movb $3,[0x8bb5]` is a BYTE store, but
    typed WORD -> `= 3` wrote 0x0003, clobbering the adjacent renderer-index byte 0x8bb6 -> the dirty-walk
    (209e) re-paint dispatched the WRONG renderer for the SMOKE element -> its state renderer 6d45 never
    re-ran -> the LED kept the stale (checked) render.  (Identical to patch 318's SKY 0x8ba9->0x8baa.)
  - SMOKE checkbox STATE flag 0x8b4f (DAT_2000_4b4f): asm 0x6c1d `xorb`/0x6c2a `cmpb` are BYTE ops, typed
    WORD -> the word read/write pulls in adjacent byte 0x8b50.  (Identical to patch 318's SKY 0x8b46.)
Retype both to undefined1 (BYTE), matching the asm and patches 318/319.  DAT_2000_4b4f is used only by
the SMOKE toggle 6c1d (the paint 6d45 + init 6ef5 read byte[0x8b4f] directly); DAT_2000_4bb5 is only ever
written `= 3`.  SETTINGS-click-only -> behaviour-neutral for all non-SMOKE flows.

Verified: SMOKE-EFFECTS toggle now AE=0 vs the genuine DOSBox reference on native AND wasm, native<->wasm
0-diff, deterministic.  Sources stay pristine (re_out/fist.c 61453e42); applies onto build/ after 386.

